turbo run test at d668fd0: 24 tasks successful. @liberty/web 72 files / 1265 tests passed; @liberty/backend 19 tests; all workspace packages green.

THE REGRESSION gpt-architect ASKED FOR BY NAME, in playback-session-authentication.test.ts, written as the six claims that would each individually have let the defect back in rather than as one assertion about an outcome:

 - a VALID request -- not a malformed one, which the schema would refuse whatever the gate did, so it could not tell a fail-closed gate from an absent one -- is answered unavailable / authentication_not_configured;
 - 503 through the envelope, with no-store;
 - the resolver is NEVER CALLED, which is the clause "Do NOT continue into content/provider resolution" asserted as a mechanism rather than as a property of the response body;
 - request.bodyUsed is FALSE at the refusal, which is the verdict's "so the absence-of-auth case cannot become a content oracle either" -- practical because the gate sits in front of readJsonBody for every branch and not for the signed-out one only;
 - the refusal is BYTE-IDENTICAL across a real title, an invented title, a malformed id and a body that is not JSON;
 - and the two events under authentication_not_configured keep DIFFERENT details, because "configure an identity store" and "your identity store is down" send an operator to different places, while both details stay caller-invariant and content-invariant.

The old test that asserted the fall-through -- "decides exactly as it did before this gate existed" -- is gone rather than skipped. It was the defect written down as an expectation.

TWO TESTS ADDED FOR THE MISATTRIBUTION FOUND WHILE DOING THIS, in watch-session.test.ts: the not-configured panel now says WHICH configuration is missing, and a deployment with no identity system is never mapped to signed-out -- there is no sign-in that could complete there, so offering one would be the dead end this task removes, wearing the label of the fix.

Lint and build recorded with the typecheck gate; this gate is the unit suite.
